<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sicuani</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sicuani is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a> Region of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, on the Vilcanota river at about 3,550 m, and the capital of Canchis Province. It lies on the route between Cusco and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-titicaca">Lake Titicaca</a>. In March 1836 an assembly of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">departments</a> of Peru met there and proclaimed the South Peruvian Republic, part of the Peru–Bolivian Confederation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sicuani.jpg" alt="Sicuani" width="320" height="107" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ant.rios2013 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PANORAMICA_SICUANI.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
